      {"bad":"The band rehearsed for the school concert. The singer and the drummer arrives first each time. Together they set up their instruments near the stage. Neither the piano nor the guitars need tuning today. The rehearsal finished right on time.","good":"The band rehearsed for the school concert. The singer and the drummer arrive first each time. Together they set up their instruments near the stage. Neither the piano nor the guitars need tuning today. The rehearsal finished right on time.","explanation":"A compound subject takes a plural verb (\"arrive\"); \"nor\" follows the nearer plural (\"need\").","sentences":[{"bad":"The band rehearsed for the school concert.","good":"The band rehearsed for the school concert."},{"bad":"The singer and the drummer arrives first each time.","good":"The singer and the drummer arrive first each time."},{"bad":"Together they set up their instruments near the stage.","good":"Together they set up their instruments near the stage."},{"bad":"Neither the piano nor the guitars need tuning today.","good":"Neither the piano nor the guitars need tuning today."},{"bad":"The rehearsal finished right on time.","good":"The rehearsal finished right on time."}]},
