    "3.6": [
      {"bad":"Two friends swapped books after class. \"This one is my,\" said Sam. Anna held up a blue notebook. \"And this is your,\" she replied with a smile. They promised to read both by Friday.","good":"Two friends swapped books after class. \"This one is mine,\" said Sam. Anna held up a blue notebook. \"And this is yours,\" she replied with a smile. They promised to read both by Friday.","explanation":"A possessive determiner needs a noun; standing alone it becomes a pronoun: \"mine\", \"yours\".","sentences":[{"bad":"Two friends swapped books after class.","good":"Two friends swapped books after class."},{"bad":"\"This one is my,\" said Sam.","good":"\"This one is mine,\" said Sam."},{"bad":"Anna held up a blue notebook.","good":"Anna held up a blue notebook."},{"bad":"\"And this is your,\" she replied with a smile.","good":"\"And this is yours,\" she replied with a smile."},{"bad":"They promised to read both by Friday.","good":"They promised to read both by Friday."}]},
      {"bad":"The children sorted their toys into two boxes. \"These are her and those are his,\" said the mother. Each box had a label on the side. \"Remember, this box is our,\" she added. The room was tidy within an hour.","good":"The children sorted their toys into two boxes. \"These are hers and those are his,\" said the mother. Each box had a label on the side. \"Remember, this box is ours,\" she added. The room was tidy within an hour.","explanation":"Use possessive pronouns \"hers\", \"ours\" when no noun follows.","sentences":[{"bad":"The children sorted their toys into two boxes.","good":"The children sorted their toys into two boxes."},{"bad":"\"These are her and those are his,\" said the mother.","good":"\"These are hers and those are his,\" said the mother."},{"bad":"Each box had a label on the side.","good":"Each box had a label on the side."},{"bad":"\"Remember, this box is our,\" she added.","good":"\"Remember, this box is ours,\" she added."},{"bad":"The room was tidy within an hour.","good":"The room was tidy within an hour."}]},
      {"bad":"Two neighbours compared their gardens. \"My roses are lovely, but your are taller,\" said one. They walked along the fence together. \"That bench is their,\" the other noted. They agreed to share the space.","good":"Two neighbours compared their gardens. \"My roses are lovely, but yours are taller,\" said one. They walked along the fence together. \"That bench is theirs,\" the other noted. They agreed to share the space.","explanation":"Possessive pronouns replace the whole phrase: \"yours\", \"theirs\".","sentences":[{"bad":"Two neighbours compared their gardens.","good":"Two neighbours compared their gardens."},{"bad":"\"My roses are lovely, but your are taller,\" said one.","good":"\"My roses are lovely, but yours are taller,\" said one."},{"bad":"They walked along the fence together.","good":"They walked along the fence together."},{"bad":"\"That bench is their,\" the other noted.","good":"\"That bench is theirs,\" the other noted."},{"bad":"They agreed to share the space.","good":"They agreed to share the space."}]},
      {"bad":"The students collected their projects. \"Is this pen your?\" asked Ben. Mia shook her head. \"Mine is over there; this one is her,\" she said. The owner soon claimed it.","good":"The students collected their projects. \"Is this pen yours?\" asked Ben. Mia shook her head. \"Mine is over there; this one is hers,\" she said. The owner soon claimed it.","explanation":"Use \"yours\" and \"hers\" when the noun is left out.","sentences":[{"bad":"The students collected their projects.","good":"The students collected their projects."},{"bad":"\"Is this pen your?\" asked Ben.","good":"\"Is this pen yours?\" asked Ben."},{"bad":"Mia shook her head.","good":"Mia shook her head."},{"bad":"\"Mine is over there; this one is her,\" she said.","good":"\"Mine is over there; this one is hers,\" she said."},{"bad":"The owner soon claimed it.","good":"The owner soon claimed it."}]},
      {"bad":"The family divided the old photographs. \"These are our and those are their,\" said Mother. Each person received a small bundle. \"Keep mine safe and I will keep your,\" she added. The photos were treasured by everyone.","good":"The family divided the old photographs. \"These are ours and those are theirs,\" said Mother. Each person received a small bundle. \"Keep mine safe and I will keep yours,\" she added. The photos were treasured by everyone.","explanation":"Without a following noun, use \"ours\", \"theirs\", \"yours\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The family divided the old photographs.","good":"The family divided the old photographs."},{"bad":"\"These are our and those are their,\" said Mother.","good":"\"These are ours and those are theirs,\" said Mother."},{"bad":"Each person received a small bundle.","good":"Each person received a small bundle."},{"bad":"\"Keep mine safe and I will keep your,\" she added.","good":"\"Keep mine safe and I will keep yours,\" she added."},{"bad":"The photos were treasured by everyone.","good":"The photos were treasured by everyone."}]}
