    "3.7": [
      {"bad":"We planned a picnic for the weekend. I will bring some fruit and some juice. My sister offered to make sandwiches. \"Do we have some napkins?\" she asked. I checked the cupboard and found a pack.","good":"We planned a picnic for the weekend. I will bring some fruit and some juice. My sister offered to make sandwiches. \"Do we have any napkins?\" she asked. I checked the cupboard and found a pack.","explanation":"Use \"some\" in positive statements and \"any\" in questions.","sentences":[{"bad":"We planned a picnic for the weekend.","good":"We planned a picnic for the weekend."},{"bad":"I will bring some fruit and some juice.","good":"I will bring some fruit and some juice."},{"bad":"My sister offered to make sandwiches.","good":"My sister offered to make sandwiches."},{"bad":"\"Do we have some napkins?\" she asked.","good":"\"Do we have any napkins?\" she asked."},{"bad":"I checked the cupboard and found a pack.","good":"I checked the cupboard and found a pack."}]},
      {"bad":"The fridge was almost empty on Monday. We did not have some milk left. I made a shopping list at once. I bought some bread and some cheese. The fridge looked much better by evening.","good":"The fridge was almost empty on Monday. We did not have any milk left. I made a shopping list at once. I bought some bread and some cheese. The fridge looked much better by evening.","explanation":"Negatives take \"any\": \"did not have any milk\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The fridge was almost empty on Monday.","good":"The fridge was almost empty on Monday."},{"bad":"We did not have some milk left.","good":"We did not have any milk left."},{"bad":"I made a shopping list at once.","good":"I made a shopping list at once."},{"bad":"I bought some bread and some cheese.","good":"I bought some bread and some cheese."},{"bad":"The fridge looked much better by evening.","good":"The fridge looked much better by evening."}]},
      {"bad":"The children asked for a story before bed. \"Are there some books about dragons?\" they asked. I found one on the top shelf. \"There are some pictures on every page,\" I said. They listened quietly to the whole tale.","good":"The children asked for a story before bed. \"Are there any books about dragons?\" they asked. I found one on the top shelf. \"There are some pictures on every page,\" I said. They listened quietly to the whole tale.","explanation":"Use \"any\" in questions and \"some\" in positive statements.","sentences":[{"bad":"The children asked for a story before bed.","good":"The children asked for a story before bed."},{"bad":"\"Are there some books about dragons?\" they asked.","good":"\"Are there any books about dragons?\" they asked."},{"bad":"I found one on the top shelf.","good":"I found one on the top shelf."},{"bad":"\"There are some pictures on every page,\" I said.","good":"\"There are some pictures on every page,\" I said."},{"bad":"They listened quietly to the whole tale.","good":"They listened quietly to the whole tale."}]},
      {"bad":"The office was quiet on Friday afternoon. \"Has some post arrived today?\" asked the manager. The clerk checked the front desk. \"There are some letters for you,\" she replied. The manager read them before leaving.","good":"The office was quiet on Friday afternoon. \"Has any post arrived today?\" asked the manager. The clerk checked the front desk. \"There are some letters for you,\" she replied. The manager read them before leaving.","explanation":"Questions take \"any\"; positive statements take \"some\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The office was quiet on Friday afternoon.","good":"The office was quiet on Friday afternoon."},{"bad":"\"Has some post arrived today?\" asked the manager.","good":"\"Has any post arrived today?\" asked the manager."},{"bad":"The clerk checked the front desk.","good":"The clerk checked the front desk."},{"bad":"\"There are some letters for you,\" she replied.","good":"\"There are some letters for you,\" she replied."},{"bad":"The manager read them before leaving.","good":"The manager read them before leaving."}]},
      {"bad":"We were preparing for the visitors. \"We do not have some chairs left,\" said my father. He fetched two from the garage. \"Could you also bring some glasses?\" asked my mother. Everything was ready in time.","good":"We were preparing for the visitors. \"We do not have any chairs left,\" said my father. He fetched two from the garage. \"Could you also bring some glasses?\" asked my mother. Everything was ready in time.","explanation":"Negatives use \"any\"; requests and positives use \"some\".","sentences":[{"bad":"We were preparing for the visitors.","good":"We were preparing for the visitors."},{"bad":"\"We do not have some chairs left,\" said my father.","good":"\"We do not have any chairs left,\" said my father."},{"bad":"He fetched two from the garage.","good":"He fetched two from the garage."},{"bad":"\"Could you also bring some glasses?\" asked my mother.","good":"\"Could you also bring some glasses?\" asked my mother."},{"bad":"Everything was ready in time.","good":"Everything was ready in time."}]}
