      {"bad":"The class planned their end-of-year trip. Each options was discussed for a long time. The teacher wrote the ideas on the board. The whole class agreed on another places to visit. The trip was booked before the holiday.","good":"The class planned their end-of-year trip. Each option was discussed for a long time. The teacher wrote the ideas on the board. The whole class agreed on another place to visit. The trip was booked before the holiday.","explanation":"\"Each option\" and \"another place\" are singular.","sentences":[{"bad":"The class planned their end-of-year trip.","good":"The class planned their end-of-year trip."},{"bad":"Each options was discussed for a long time.","good":"Each option was discussed for a long time."},{"bad":"The teacher wrote the ideas on the board.","good":"The teacher wrote the ideas on the board."},{"bad":"The whole class agreed on another places to visit.","good":"The whole class agreed on another place to visit."},{"bad":"The trip was booked before the holiday.","good":"The trip was booked before the holiday."}]},
