      {"bad":"The whole class helped decorate the hall. Myself painted the big banner. Others arranged the chairs and tables. He and myself hung the balloons. The hall looked wonderful for the party.","good":"The whole class helped decorate the hall. I painted the big banner. Others arranged the chairs and tables. He and I hung the balloons. The hall looked wonderful for the party.","explanation":"A reflexive cannot be the subject; use \"I\" for the subject.","sentences":[{"bad":"The whole class helped decorate the hall.","good":"The whole class helped decorate the hall."},{"bad":"Myself painted the big banner.","good":"I painted the big banner."},{"bad":"Others arranged the chairs and tables.","good":"Others arranged the chairs and tables."},{"bad":"He and myself hung the balloons.","good":"He and I hung the balloons."},{"bad":"The hall looked wonderful for the party.","good":"The hall looked wonderful for the party."}]},
      {"bad":"The project needed careful planning. Themselves finished the report on time. The manager praised the whole team. Herself checked every figure twice. The report was submitted before the deadline.","good":"The project needed careful planning. They finished the report on time. The manager praised the whole team. She checked every figure twice. The report was submitted before the deadline.","explanation":"Use ordinary subject pronouns \"They\" and \"She\", not reflexives.","sentences":[{"bad":"The project needed careful planning.","good":"The project needed careful planning."},{"bad":"Themselves finished the report on time.","good":"They finished the report on time."},{"bad":"The manager praised the whole team.","good":"The manager praised the whole team."},{"bad":"Herself checked every figure twice.","good":"She checked every figure twice."},{"bad":"The report was submitted before the deadline.","good":"The report was submitted before the deadline."}]},
