      {"bad":"The workers finished the repairs quickly. Themselves fixed the broken fence. The owner inspected the work. Myself thanked them for their effort. The fence looked as good as new.","good":"The workers finished the repairs quickly. They fixed the broken fence. The owner inspected the work. I thanked them for their effort. The fence looked as good as new.","explanation":"Use ordinary subject pronouns \"They\" and \"I\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The workers finished the repairs quickly.","good":"The workers finished the repairs quickly."},{"bad":"Themselves fixed the broken fence.","good":"They fixed the broken fence."},{"bad":"The owner inspected the work.","good":"The owner inspected the work."},{"bad":"Myself thanked them for their effort.","good":"I thanked them for their effort."},{"bad":"The fence looked as good as new.","good":"The fence looked as good as new."}]}
