      {"bad":"The singer rehearsed with the band. She may sings the new song tonight. The band has practised for weeks. They have wrote two new pieces. In fact, the concert sold out quickly.","good":"The singer rehearsed with the band. She may sing the new song tonight. The band has practised for weeks. They have written two new pieces. In fact, the concert sold out quickly.","explanation":"After \"may\" use \"sing\"; after \"have\" use \"written\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The singer rehearsed with the band.","good":"The singer rehearsed with the band."},{"bad":"She may sings the new song tonight.","good":"She may sing the new song tonight."},{"bad":"The band has practised for weeks.","good":"The band has practised for weeks."},{"bad":"They have wrote two new pieces.","good":"They have written two new pieces."},{"bad":"In fact, the concert sold out quickly.","good":"In fact, the concert sold out quickly."}]},
      {"bad":"The kitchen prepared for the dinner rush. The chef must washes the vegetables first. The staff have set the tables neatly. They have went through the whole menu twice. Then the doors opened at six.","good":"The kitchen prepared for the dinner rush. The chef must wash the vegetables first. The staff have set the tables neatly. They have gone through the whole menu twice. Then the doors opened at six.","explanation":"After \"must\" use \"wash\"; after \"have\" use \"gone\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The kitchen prepared for the dinner rush.","good":"The kitchen prepared for the dinner rush."},{"bad":"The chef must washes the vegetables first.","good":"The chef must wash the vegetables first."},{"bad":"The staff have set the tables neatly.","good":"The staff have set the tables neatly."},{"bad":"They have went through the whole menu twice.","good":"They have gone through the whole menu twice."},{"bad":"Then the doors opened at six.","good":"Then the doors opened at six."}]}
