      {"bad":"The shop opened early on Saturday. The shelves full of fresh produce. Customers filled their baskets. The prices very fair for the quality. The shop sold out by noon.","good":"The shop opened early on Saturday. The shelves were full of fresh produce. Customers filled their baskets. The prices were very fair for the quality. The shop sold out by noon.","explanation":"Add the verb \"were\" to each clause.","sentences":[{"bad":"The shop opened early on Saturday.","good":"The shop opened early on Saturday."},{"bad":"The shelves full of fresh produce.","good":"The shelves were full of fresh produce."},{"bad":"Customers filled their baskets.","good":"Customers filled their baskets."},{"bad":"The prices very fair for the quality.","good":"The prices were very fair for the quality."},{"bad":"The shop sold out by noon.","good":"The shop sold out by noon."}]},
