      {"bad":"The school arranged a music competition. Three prizes gave to the best singers. The audience cheered loudly. The final song write by a student. Everyone left with a smile.","good":"The school arranged a music competition. Three prizes were given to the best singers. The audience cheered loudly. The final song was written by a student. Everyone left with a smile.","explanation":"Use \"were given\" and \"was written\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The school arranged a music competition.","good":"The school arranged a music competition."},{"bad":"Three prizes gave to the best singers.","good":"Three prizes were given to the best singers."},{"bad":"The audience cheered loudly.","good":"The audience cheered loudly."},{"bad":"The final song write by a student.","good":"The final song was written by a student."},{"bad":"Everyone left with a smile.","good":"Everyone left with a smile."}]},
