      {"bad":"The committee reviewed the new rules. The rules approve at last week's meeting. Staff received a written summary. The changes announce to everyone by email. The new rules start in June.","good":"The committee reviewed the new rules. The rules were approved at last week's meeting. Staff received a written summary. The changes were announced to everyone by email. The new rules start in June.","explanation":"Use \"were approved\" and \"were announced\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The committee reviewed the new rules.","good":"The committee reviewed the new rules."},{"bad":"The rules approve at last week's meeting.","good":"The rules were approved at last week's meeting."},{"bad":"Staff received a written summary.","good":"Staff received a written summary."},{"bad":"The changes announce to everyone by email.","good":"The changes were announced to everyone by email."},{"bad":"The new rules start in June.","good":"The new rules start in June."}]},
