    "6.14": [
      {"bad":"My brother saved his pocket money carefully. He does not have no money left now. He spent it on a new bicycle. He does not want nothing else for his birthday. He rides it every day.","good":"My brother saved his pocket money carefully. He does not have any money left now. He spent it on a new bicycle. He does not want anything else for his birthday. He rides it every day.","explanation":"Standard English uses one negative: \"not... any\".","sentences":[{"bad":"My brother saved his pocket money carefully.","good":"My brother saved his pocket money carefully."},{"bad":"He does not have no money left now.","good":"He does not have any money left now."},{"bad":"He spent it on a new bicycle.","good":"He spent it on a new bicycle."},{"bad":"He does not want nothing else for his birthday.","good":"He does not want anything else for his birthday."},{"bad":"He rides it every day.","good":"He rides it every day."}]},
      {"bad":"The team played an away match on Sunday. They did not score no goals in the first half. The coach gave them a firm talk. They did not lose no confidence. In the end, they won the second half easily.","good":"The team played an away match on Sunday. They did not score any goals in the first half. The coach gave them a firm talk. They did not lose any confidence. In the end, they won the second half easily.","explanation":"Use \"any\" after \"not\", not a second negative.","sentences":[{"bad":"The team played an away match on Sunday.","good":"The team played an away match on Sunday."},{"bad":"They did not score no goals in the first half.","good":"They did not score any goals in the first half."},{"bad":"The coach gave them a firm talk.","good":"The coach gave them a firm talk."},{"bad":"They did not lose no confidence.","good":"They did not lose any confidence."},{"bad":"In the end, they won the second half easily.","good":"In the end, they won the second half easily."}]},
      {"bad":"The children tidied the classroom after school. Nobody did not help with the chairs. They stacked them by the wall. They did not leave nothing on the floor. The room was spotless in an hour.","good":"The children tidied the classroom after school. Nobody helped with the chairs. They stacked them by the wall. They did not leave anything on the floor. The room was spotless in an hour.","explanation":"\"Nobody\" is already negative; do not add \"did not\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The children tidied the classroom after school.","good":"The children tidied the classroom after school."},{"bad":"Nobody did not help with the chairs.","good":"Nobody helped with the chairs."},{"bad":"They stacked them by the wall.","good":"They stacked them by the wall."},{"bad":"They did not leave nothing on the floor.","good":"They did not leave anything on the floor."},{"bad":"The room was spotless in an hour.","good":"The room was spotless in an hour."}]},
      {"bad":"The shop stayed open late on Friday. There were not no customers all evening. The owner read a book behind the counter. She did not serve nobody after nine. She closed the shop at ten.","good":"The shop stayed open late on Friday. There were no customers all evening. The owner read a book behind the counter. She did not serve anyone after nine. She closed the shop at ten.","explanation":"Use \"no\" or \"not... any\", never both.","sentences":[{"bad":"The shop stayed open late on Friday.","good":"The shop stayed open late on Friday."},{"bad":"There were not no customers all evening.","good":"There were no customers all evening."},{"bad":"The owner read a book behind the counter.","good":"The owner read a book behind the counter."},{"bad":"She did not serve nobody after nine.","good":"She did not serve anyone after nine."},{"bad":"She closed the shop at ten.","good":"She closed the shop at ten."}]},
      {"bad":"The travellers set off early in the morning. They did not have no maps for the route. They followed the road signs instead. They did not meet nobody on the way. By noon, they reached the coast.","good":"The travellers set off early in the morning. They did not have any maps for the route. They followed the road signs instead. They did not meet anybody on the way. By noon, they reached the coast.","explanation":"After \"not\", use \"any\"/\"anybody\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The travellers set off early in the morning.","good":"The travellers set off early in the morning."},{"bad":"They did not have no maps for the route.","good":"They did not have any maps for the route."},{"bad":"They followed the road signs instead.","good":"They followed the road signs instead."},{"bad":"They did not meet nobody on the way.","good":"They did not meet anybody on the way."},{"bad":"By noon, they reached the coast.","good":"By noon, they reached the coast."}]}
    ],
    "6.15": [
      {"bad":"The children were getting ready for bed. \"Don't goes upstairs yet,\" said their mother. She wanted them to brush their teeth first. \"Washes your hands too,\" she added. They were in bed by eight.","good":"The children were getting ready for bed. \"Don't go upstairs yet,\" said their mother. She wanted them to brush their teeth first. \"Wash your hands too,\" she added. They were in bed by eight.","explanation":"Imperatives use the base form: \"don't go\", \"wash\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The children were getting ready for bed.","good":"The children were getting ready for bed."},{"bad":"\"Don't goes upstairs yet,\" said their mother.","good":"\"Don't go upstairs yet,\" said their mother."},{"bad":"She wanted them to brush their teeth first.","good":"She wanted them to brush their teeth first."},{"bad":"\"Washes your hands too,\" she added.","good":"\"Wash your hands too,\" she added."},{"bad":"They were in bed by eight.","good":"They were in bed by eight."}]},
      {"bad":"The coach gathered the players on the field. \"Listens carefully to the plan,\" he said. He pointed to the far goal. \"Don't loses your positions,\" he warned. The team played well that day.","good":"The coach gathered the players on the field. \"Listen carefully to the plan,\" he said. He pointed to the far goal. \"Don't lose your positions,\" he warned. The team played well that day.","explanation":"Use the base forms \"listen\" and \"don't lose\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The coach gathered the players on the field.","good":"The coach gathered the players on the field."},{"bad":"\"Listens carefully to the plan,\" he said.","good":"\"Listen carefully to the plan,\" he said."},{"bad":"He pointed to the far goal.","good":"He pointed to the far goal."},{"bad":"\"Don't loses your positions,\" he warned.","good":"\"Don't lose your positions,\" he warned."},{"bad":"The team played well that day.","good":"The team played well that day."}]},
      {"bad":"The teacher handed out the test papers. \"Please writes your name at the top,\" she said. The class began at once. \"Don't talks during the test,\" she added. Everyone worked quietly.","good":"The teacher handed out the test papers. \"Please write your name at the top,\" she said. The class began at once. \"Don't talk during the test,\" she added. Everyone worked quietly.","explanation":"Imperatives use \"write\" and \"don't talk\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The teacher handed out the test papers.","good":"The teacher handed out the test papers."},{"bad":"\"Please writes your name at the top,\" she said.","good":"\"Please write your name at the top,\" she said."},{"bad":"The class began at once.","good":"The class began at once."},{"bad":"\"Don't talks during the test,\" she added.","good":"\"Don't talk during the test,\" she added."},{"bad":"Everyone worked quietly.","good":"Everyone worked quietly."}]},
      {"bad":"The hikers reached a steep path. \"Takes small steps here,\" said the guide. The rocks were wet from the rain. \"Don't rushes,\" he warned the group. They reached the top safely.","good":"The hikers reached a steep path. \"Take small steps here,\" said the guide. The rocks were wet from the rain. \"Don't rush,\" he warned the group. They reached the top safely.","explanation":"Use the base forms \"take\" and \"don't rush\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The hikers reached a steep path.","good":"The hikers reached a steep path."},{"bad":"\"Takes small steps here,\" said the guide.","good":"\"Take small steps here,\" said the guide."},{"bad":"The rocks were wet from the rain.","good":"The rocks were wet from the rain."},{"bad":"\"Don't rushes,\" he warned the group.","good":"\"Don't rush,\" he warned the group."},{"bad":"They reached the top safely.","good":"They reached the top safely."}]},
      {"bad":"The chef was preparing the soup. \"Tastes it before serving,\" she told the helper. The helper added a little salt. \"Don't forgets the pepper,\" the chef added. The soup was perfect.","good":"The chef was preparing the soup. \"Taste it before serving,\" she told the helper. The helper added a little salt. \"Don't forget the pepper,\" the chef added. The soup was perfect.","explanation":"Imperatives use \"taste\" and \"don't forget\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The chef was preparing the soup.","good":"The chef was preparing the soup."},{"bad":"\"Tastes it before serving,\" she told the helper.","good":"\"Taste it before serving,\" she told the helper."},{"bad":"The helper added a little salt.","good":"The helper added a little salt."},{"bad":"\"Don't forgets the pepper,\" the chef added.","good":"\"Don't forget the pepper,\" the chef added."},{"bad":"The soup was perfect.","good":"The soup was perfect."}]}
    ],
    "6.16": [
      {"bad":"The garden needs a lot of water in summer. If I will water the plants daily, they will survive. The forecast promises a hot week. If it will rain tomorrow, I will stay indoors. The flowers should be fine either way.","good":"The garden needs a lot of water in summer. If I water the plants daily, they will survive. The forecast promises a hot week. If it rains tomorrow, I will stay indoors. The flowers should be fine either way.","explanation":"In real conditionals, use the present tense in the if-clause, not \"will\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The garden needs a lot of water in summer.","good":"The garden needs a lot of water in summer."},{"bad":"If I will water the plants daily, they will survive.","good":"If I water the plants daily, they will survive."},{"bad":"The forecast promises a hot week.","good":"The forecast promises a hot week."},{"bad":"If it will rain tomorrow, I will stay indoors.","good":"If it rains tomorrow, I will stay indoors."},{"bad":"The flowers should be fine either way.","good":"The flowers should be fine either way."}]},
      {"bad":"The team needs to win the next match. If they will play well, they will reach the final. The coach is confident about the squad. If the captain will return, the team will be stronger. The final is on Saturday.","good":"The team needs to win the next match. If they play well, they will reach the final. The coach is confident about the squad. If the captain returns, the team will be stronger. The final is on Saturday.","explanation":"Use \"if they play\" and \"if the captain returns\" (present tense).","sentences":[{"bad":"The team needs to win the next match.","good":"The team needs to win the next match."},{"bad":"If they will play well, they will reach the final.","good":"If they play well, they will reach the final."},{"bad":"The coach is confident about the squad.","good":"The coach is confident about the squad."},{"bad":"If the captain will return, the team will be stronger.","good":"If the captain returns, the team will be stronger."},{"bad":"The final is on Saturday.","good":"The final is on Saturday."}]},
      {"bad":"The family plans a trip to the mountains. If the weather will be good, we will drive up on Friday. The cabin is already booked. If we will leave early, we will avoid the traffic. The journey should take four hours.","good":"The family plans a trip to the mountains. If the weather is good, we will drive up on Friday. The cabin is already booked. If we leave early, we will avoid the traffic. The journey should take four hours.","explanation":"Use the present tense in the if-clause: \"is\", \"leave\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The family plans a trip to the mountains.","good":"The family plans a trip to the mountains."},{"bad":"If the weather will be good, we will drive up on Friday.","good":"If the weather is good, we will drive up on Friday."},{"bad":"The cabin is already booked.","good":"The cabin is already booked."},{"bad":"If we will leave early, we will avoid the traffic.","good":"If we leave early, we will avoid the traffic."},{"bad":"The journey should take four hours.","good":"The journey should take four hours."}]},
      {"bad":"The students are revising for the exam. If she will study hard, she will pass easily. The teacher gave them a study plan. If they will follow it, they will do well. The exam is next Tuesday.","good":"The students are revising for the exam. If she studies hard, she will pass easily. The teacher gave them a study plan. If they follow it, they will do well. The exam is next Tuesday.","explanation":"Use \"studies\" and \"follow\" in the if-clause, not \"will\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The students are revising for the exam.","good":"The students are revising for the exam."},{"bad":"If she will study hard, she will pass easily.","good":"If she studies hard, she will pass easily."},{"bad":"The teacher gave them a study plan.","good":"The teacher gave them a study plan."},{"bad":"If they will follow it, they will do well.","good":"If they follow it, they will do well."},{"bad":"The exam is next Tuesday.","good":"The exam is next Tuesday."}]},
      {"bad":"The business hopes to grow this year. If the sales will increase, they will hire more staff. The manager prepared a budget. If they will open a new branch, they will need more space. The plan goes to the board in June.","good":"The business hopes to grow this year. If the sales increase, they will hire more staff. The manager prepared a budget. If they open a new branch, they will need more space. The plan goes to the board in June.","explanation":"Use present-tense verbs in the if-clause: \"increase\", \"open\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The business hopes to grow this year.","good":"The business hopes to grow this year."},{"bad":"If the sales will increase, they will hire more staff.","good":"If the sales increase, they will hire more staff."},{"bad":"The manager prepared a budget.","good":"The manager prepared a budget."},{"bad":"If they will open a new branch, they will need more space.","good":"If they open a new branch, they will need more space."},{"bad":"The plan goes to the board in June.","good":"The plan goes to the board in June."}]}
    ],
    "6.17": [
      {"bad":"The weather was cold during the holiday. I wish I was somewhere warm. The heating was broken all week. If I was you, I would complain to the hotel. We made the best of a difficult week.","good":"The weather was cold during the holiday. I wish I were somewhere warm. The heating was broken all week. If I were you, I would complain to the hotel. We made the best of a difficult week.","explanation":"In \"wish\" and hypotheticals, use \"were\" for all subjects.","sentences":[{"bad":"The weather was cold during the holiday.","good":"The weather was cold during the holiday."},{"bad":"I wish I was somewhere warm.","good":"I wish I were somewhere warm."},{"bad":"The heating was broken all week.","good":"The heating was broken all week."},{"bad":"If I was you, I would complain to the hotel.","good":"If I were you, I would complain to the hotel."},{"bad":"We made the best of a difficult week.","good":"We made the best of a difficult week."}]},
      {"bad":"My friend is studying medicine. She wishes she was already a doctor. The course takes several years. If she was allowed, she would start work tomorrow. She works very hard in the meantime.","good":"My friend is studying medicine. She wishes she were already a doctor. The course takes several years. If she were allowed, she would start work tomorrow. She works very hard in the meantime.","explanation":"Use \"were\" in \"wish\" and in the hypothetical clause.","sentences":[{"bad":"My friend is studying medicine.","good":"My friend is studying medicine."},{"bad":"She wishes she was already a doctor.","good":"She wishes she were already a doctor."},{"bad":"The course takes several years.","good":"The course takes several years."},{"bad":"If she was allowed, she would start work tomorrow.","good":"If she were allowed, she would start work tomorrow."},{"bad":"She works very hard in the meantime.","good":"She works very hard in the meantime."}]},
      {"bad":"The team missed the final by one point. The coach wishes he was still in the competition. The players trained hard all season. If he was able, he would replay the last minute. They plan to try again next year.","good":"The team missed the final by one point. The coach wishes he were still in the competition. The players trained hard all season. If he were able, he would replay the last minute. They plan to try again next year.","explanation":"Use the subjunctive \"were\" after \"wish\" and \"if\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The team missed the final by one point.","good":"The team missed the final by one point."},{"bad":"The coach wishes he was still in the competition.","good":"The coach wishes he were still in the competition."},{"bad":"The players trained hard all season.","good":"The players trained hard all season."},{"bad":"If he was able, he would replay the last minute.","good":"If he were able, he would replay the last minute."},{"bad":"They plan to try again next year.","good":"They plan to try again next year."}]},
      {"bad":"The old house is full of character. I wish it was a little warmer inside. The rooms are spacious and bright. If it was cheaper, we would buy it at once. For now, we simply enjoy visiting.","good":"The old house is full of character. I wish it were a little warmer inside. The rooms are spacious and bright. If it were cheaper, we would buy it at once. For now, we simply enjoy visiting.","explanation":"Hypotheticals take \"were\": \"I wish it were\", \"if it were\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The old house is full of character.","good":"The old house is full of character."},{"bad":"I wish it was a little warmer inside.","good":"I wish it were a little warmer inside."},{"bad":"The rooms are spacious and bright.","good":"The rooms are spacious and bright."},{"bad":"If it was cheaper, we would buy it at once.","good":"If it were cheaper, we would buy it at once."},{"bad":"For now, we simply enjoy visiting.","good":"For now, we simply enjoy visiting."}]},
      {"bad":"The exam results arrive next week. She wishes she was less nervous about them. She has prepared for months. If she was calmer, she would sleep better. Her friends keep her cheerful.","good":"The exam results arrive next week. She wishes she were less nervous about them. She has prepared for months. If she were calmer, she would sleep better. Her friends keep her cheerful.","explanation":"Use \"were\" after \"wish\" and in the hypothetical if-clause.","sentences":[{"bad":"The exam results arrive next week.","good":"The exam results arrive next week."},{"bad":"She wishes she was less nervous about them.","good":"She wishes she were less nervous about them."},{"bad":"She has prepared for months.","good":"She has prepared for months."},{"bad":"If she was calmer, she would sleep better.","good":"If she were calmer, she would sleep better."},{"bad":"Her friends keep her cheerful.","good":"Her friends keep her cheerful."}]}
    ],
    "6.18": [
      {"bad":"My sister called me from the station. She said me the train was delayed. I offered to wait for her. She said she would arrive by six. We met at the café nearby.","good":"My sister called me from the station. She told me the train was delayed. I offered to wait for her. She said she would arrive by six. We met at the café nearby.","explanation":"Use \"tell + person\" and \"say + clause\" (no \"me\" after \"said\" here).","sentences":[{"bad":"My sister called me from the station.","good":"My sister called me from the station."},{"bad":"She said me the train was delayed.","good":"She told me the train was delayed."},{"bad":"I offered to wait for her.","good":"I offered to wait for her."},{"bad":"She said she would arrive by six.","good":"She said she would arrive by six."},{"bad":"We met at the café nearby.","good":"We met at the café nearby."}]},
      {"bad":"The teacher spoke to the class. She told that the test would be on Friday. The pupils wrote the date down. She also told us to revise the first chapter. The test was fair and short.","good":"The teacher spoke to the class. She said that the test would be on Friday. The pupils wrote the date down. She also told us to revise the first chapter. The test was fair and short.","explanation":"\"Say\" introduces a clause; \"tell\" needs a person object.","sentences":[{"bad":"The teacher spoke to the class.","good":"The teacher spoke to the class."},{"bad":"She told that the test would be on Friday.","good":"She said that the test would be on Friday."},{"bad":"The pupils wrote the date down.","good":"The pupils wrote the date down."},{"bad":"She also told us to revise the first chapter.","good":"She also told us to revise the first chapter."},{"bad":"The test was fair and short.","good":"The test was fair and short."}]},
      {"bad":"My colleague updated me about the meeting. He said me the project was on track. We reviewed the schedule together. He explained that the deadline had moved. The new deadline suits everyone.","good":"My colleague updated me about the meeting. He told me the project was on track. We reviewed the schedule together. He explained that the deadline had moved. The new deadline suits everyone.","explanation":"Use \"told me\" rather than \"said me\".","sentences":[{"bad":"My colleague updated me about the meeting.","good":"My colleague updated me about the meeting."},{"bad":"He said me the project was on track.","good":"He told me the project was on track."},{"bad":"We reviewed the schedule together.","good":"We reviewed the schedule together."},{"bad":"He explained that the deadline had moved.","good":"He explained that the deadline had moved."},{"bad":"The new deadline suits everyone.","good":"The new deadline suits everyone."}]},
      {"bad":"The guide welcomed us to the museum. She said us the tour would last an hour. We followed her through the main hall. She explained that photography was not allowed. The tour ended by the gift shop.","good":"The guide welcomed us to the museum. She told us the tour would last an hour. We followed her through the main hall. She explained that photography was not allowed. The tour ended by the gift shop.","explanation":"Use \"told us\" (person object) for reported information.","sentences":[{"bad":"The guide welcomed us to the museum.","good":"The guide welcomed us to the museum."},{"bad":"She said us the tour would last an hour.","good":"She told us the tour would last an hour."},{"bad":"We followed her through the main hall.","good":"We followed her through the main hall."},{"bad":"She explained that photography was not allowed.","good":"She explained that photography was not allowed."},{"bad":"The tour ended by the gift shop.","good":"The tour ended by the gift shop."}]},
      {"bad":"My neighbour asked about the parcel. He told that it had arrived this morning. I thanked him for letting me know. He also told me he had signed for it. I collected it after lunch.","good":"My neighbour asked about the parcel. He said that it had arrived this morning. I thanked him for letting me know. He also told me he had signed for it. I collected it after lunch.","explanation":"\"Said that...\" for a clause; \"told me (that)...\" with a person.","sentences":[{"bad":"My neighbour asked about the parcel.","good":"My neighbour asked about the parcel."},{"bad":"He told that it had arrived this morning.","good":"He said that it had arrived this morning."},{"bad":"I thanked him for letting me know.","good":"I thanked him for letting me know."},{"bad":"He also told me he had signed for it.","good":"He also told me he had signed for it."},{"bad":"I collected it after lunch.","good":"I collected it after lunch."}]}
    ],
    "6.19": [
      {"bad":"The sad film moved the whole audience. It made me to cry at the end. My friend passed me a tissue. The ending let us to think about our own lives. We talked about it all the way home.","good":"The sad film moved the whole audience. It made me cry at the end. My friend passed me a tissue. The ending let us think about our own lives. We talked about it all the way home.","explanation":"\"Make\" and \"let\" take a bare infinitive: \"made me cry\", \"let us think\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The sad film moved the whole audience.","good":"The sad film moved the whole audience."},{"bad":"It made me to cry at the end.","good":"It made me cry at the end."},{"bad":"My friend passed me a tissue.","good":"My friend passed me a tissue."},{"bad":"The ending let us to think about our own lives.","good":"The ending let us think about our own lives."},{"bad":"We talked about it all the way home.","good":"We talked about it all the way home."}]},
      {"bad":"The teacher wanted the room tidy. She had the desks to move to the back. Two pupils helped at once. She made them to work quietly. The room was ready in ten minutes.","good":"The teacher wanted the room tidy. She had the desks moved to the back. Two pupils helped at once. She made them work quietly. The room was ready in ten minutes.","explanation":"Use \"had the desks moved\" (causative) and \"made them work\" (bare infinitive).","sentences":[{"bad":"The teacher wanted the room tidy.","good":"The teacher wanted the room tidy."},{"bad":"She had the desks to move to the back.","good":"She had the desks moved to the back."},{"bad":"Two pupils helped at once.","good":"Two pupils helped at once."},{"bad":"She made them to work quietly.","good":"She made them work quietly."},{"bad":"The room was ready in ten minutes.","good":"The room was ready in ten minutes."}]},
      {"bad":"My parents arranged a repair for the car. They had it to fix at the local garage. The mechanic replaced the brakes. He let us to watch the repair. The car ran smoothly afterwards.","good":"My parents arranged a repair for the car. They had it fixed at the local garage. The mechanic replaced the brakes. He let us watch the repair. The car ran smoothly afterwards.","explanation":"Use \"had it fixed\" and \"let us watch\".","sentences":[{"bad":"My parents arranged a repair for the car.","good":"My parents arranged a repair for the car."},{"bad":"They had it to fix at the local garage.","good":"They had it fixed at the local garage."},{"bad":"The mechanic replaced the brakes.","good":"The mechanic replaced the brakes."},{"bad":"He let us to watch the repair.","good":"He let us watch the repair."},{"bad":"The car ran smoothly afterwards.","good":"The car ran smoothly afterwards."}]},
      {"bad":"The gardener tidied the whole yard. She had the old tree to cut down. The yard looked much brighter. She watched the birds to return to the feeder. The garden became her favourite place.","good":"The gardener tidied the whole yard. She had the old tree cut down. The yard looked much brighter. She watched the birds return to the feeder. The garden became her favourite place.","explanation":"Use \"had the tree cut down\" and \"watched the birds return\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The gardener tidied the whole yard.","good":"The gardener tidied the whole yard."},{"bad":"She had the old tree to cut down.","good":"She had the old tree cut down."},{"bad":"The yard looked much brighter.","good":"The yard looked much brighter."},{"bad":"She watched the birds to return to the feeder.","good":"She watched the birds return to the feeder."},{"bad":"The garden became her favourite place.","good":"The garden became her favourite place."}]},
      {"bad":"The manager improved the office. She had the walls to paint a bright colour. The staff chose the shade themselves. She let them to decorate their own desks. The office felt much more welcoming.","good":"The manager improved the office. She had the walls painted a bright colour. The staff chose the shade themselves. She let them decorate their own desks. The office felt much more welcoming.","explanation":"Use \"had the walls painted\" and \"let them decorate\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The manager improved the office.","good":"The manager improved the office."},{"bad":"She had the walls to paint a bright colour.","good":"She had the walls painted a bright colour."},{"bad":"The staff chose the shade themselves.","good":"The staff chose the shade themselves."},{"bad":"She let them to decorate their own desks.","good":"She let them decorate their own desks."},{"bad":"The office felt much more welcoming.","good":"The office felt much more welcoming."}]}
    ],
    "6.20": [
      {"bad":"The committee discussed the new proposal. They suggested him to apply for the grant. He prepared the documents carefully. The chair explained him the next steps. The application was sent on time.","good":"The committee discussed the new proposal. They suggested that he apply for the grant. He prepared the documents carefully. The chair explained the next steps to him. The application was sent on time.","explanation":"\"Suggest\" takes a that-clause, and \"explain\" takes \"to + person\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The committee discussed the new proposal.","good":"The committee discussed the new proposal."},{"bad":"They suggested him to apply for the grant.","good":"They suggested that he apply for the grant."},{"bad":"He prepared the documents carefully.","good":"He prepared the documents carefully."},{"bad":"The chair explained him the next steps.","good":"The chair explained the next steps to him."},{"bad":"The application was sent on time.","good":"The application was sent on time."}]},
      {"bad":"The doctor reviewed the patient's notes. She recommended him to rest for a week. She wrote a short summary. She described him the treatment in detail. The patient left feeling reassured.","good":"The doctor reviewed the patient's notes. She recommended that he rest for a week. She wrote a short summary. She described the treatment to him in detail. The patient left feeling reassured.","explanation":"Use \"recommend that he rest\" and \"describe ... to him\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The doctor reviewed the patient's notes.","good":"The doctor reviewed the patient's notes."},{"bad":"She recommended him to rest for a week.","good":"She recommended that he rest for a week."},{"bad":"She wrote a short summary.","good":"She wrote a short summary."},{"bad":"She described him the treatment in detail.","good":"She described the treatment to him in detail."},{"bad":"The patient left feeling reassured.","good":"The patient left feeling reassured."}]},
      {"bad":"The teacher helped the new pupil. She explained him the homework rules. He wrote everything in his book. She suggested him to join the reading club. He joined the club the same week.","good":"The teacher helped the new pupil. She explained the homework rules to him. He wrote everything in his book. She suggested that he join the reading club. He joined the club the same week.","explanation":"Use \"explained ... to him\" and \"suggested that he join\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The teacher helped the new pupil.","good":"The teacher helped the new pupil."},{"bad":"She explained him the homework rules.","good":"She explained the homework rules to him."},{"bad":"He wrote everything in his book.","good":"He wrote everything in his book."},{"bad":"She suggested him to join the reading club.","good":"She suggested that he join the reading club."},{"bad":"He joined the club the same week.","good":"He joined the club the same week."}]},
      {"bad":"The manager trained the new staff. She proposed them a new schedule. They discussed it in a short meeting. She recommended them to arrive early. The schedule worked well.","good":"The manager trained the new staff. She proposed a new schedule to them. They discussed it in a short meeting. She recommended that they arrive early. The schedule worked well.","explanation":"Use \"propose ... to them\" and \"recommend that they arrive\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The manager trained the new staff.","good":"The manager trained the new staff."},{"bad":"She proposed them a new schedule.","good":"She proposed a new schedule to them."},{"bad":"They discussed it in a short meeting.","good":"They discussed it in a short meeting."},{"bad":"She recommended them to arrive early.","good":"She recommended that they arrive early."},{"bad":"The schedule worked well.","good":"The schedule worked well."}]},
      {"bad":"The guide helped the visitors. She described them the route clearly. They marked it on their maps. She suggested them to start before noon. The walk was lovely in the morning light.","good":"The guide helped the visitors. She described the route to them clearly. They marked it on their maps. She suggested that they start before noon. The walk was lovely in the morning light.","explanation":"Use \"described ... to them\" and \"suggested that they start\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The guide helped the visitors.","good":"The guide helped the visitors."},{"bad":"She described them the route clearly.","good":"She described the route to them clearly."},{"bad":"They marked it on their maps.","good":"They marked it on their maps."},{"bad":"She suggested them to start before noon.","good":"She suggested that they start before noon."},{"bad":"The walk was lovely in the morning light.","good":"The walk was lovely in the morning light."}]}
    ],
    "7.1": [
      {"bad":"My uncle collects vintage cars. He keeps a red small sports car in the garage. He polishes it every weekend. Beside it stands a wooden old chest. The garage smells of oil and polish.","good":"My uncle collects vintage cars. He keeps a small red sports car in the garage. He polishes it every weekend. Beside it stands an old wooden chest. The garage smells of oil and polish.","explanation":"Order: size before colour, age before material (\"a small red car\", \"an old wooden chest\").","sentences":[{"bad":"My uncle collects vintage cars.","good":"My uncle collects vintage cars."},{"bad":"He keeps a red small sports car in the garage.","good":"He keeps a small red sports car in the garage."},{"bad":"He polishes it every weekend.","good":"He polishes it every weekend."},{"bad":"Beside it stands a wooden old chest.","good":"Beside it stands an old wooden chest."},{"bad":"The garage smells of oil and polish.","good":"The garage smells of oil and polish."}]},
      {"bad":"The couple furnished their first flat. They bought a round modern glass table. The chairs came from a market. On the wall hangs a beautiful French landscape. The flat felt warm and inviting.","good":"The couple furnished their first flat. They bought a modern round glass table. The chairs came from a market. On the wall hangs a beautiful French landscape. The flat felt warm and inviting.","explanation":"Order: opinion, then origin, then noun; and shape before material (\"round glass\").","sentences":[{"bad":"The couple furnished their first flat.","good":"The couple furnished their first flat."},{"bad":"They bought a round modern glass table.","good":"They bought a modern round glass table."},{"bad":"The chairs came from a market.","good":"The chairs came from a market."},{"bad":"On the wall hangs a beautiful French landscape.","good":"On the wall hangs a beautiful French landscape."},{"bad":"The flat felt warm and inviting.","good":"The flat felt warm and inviting."}]},
      {"bad":"The family visited a country market. A farmer sold us some sweet green apples. We filled two large bags. My mother chose a long striped red scarf. We carried everything home happily.","good":"The family visited a country market. A farmer sold us some sweet green apples. We filled two large bags. My mother chose a long red striped scarf. We carried everything home happily.","explanation":"Colour comes before the type/pattern word: \"long red striped scarf\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The family visited a country market.","good":"The family visited a country market."},{"bad":"A farmer sold us some sweet green apples.","good":"A farmer sold us some sweet green apples."},{"bad":"We filled two large bags.","good":"We filled two large bags."},{"bad":"My mother chose a long striped red scarf.","good":"My mother chose a long red striped scarf."},{"bad":"We carried everything home happily.","good":"We carried everything home happily."}]},
      {"bad":"My grandparents moved to a coastal village. They live in a stone old cottage near the harbour. The garden runs down to the water. A friendly black Labrador greets every visitor. We visit them every summer.","good":"My grandparents moved to a coastal village. They live in an old stone cottage near the harbour. The garden runs down to the water. A friendly black Labrador greets every visitor. We visit them every summer.","explanation":"Age before material: \"an old stone cottage\".","sentences":[{"bad":"My grandparents moved to a coastal village.","good":"My grandparents moved to a coastal village."},{"bad":"They live in a stone old cottage near the harbour.","good":"They live in an old stone cottage near the harbour."},{"bad":"The garden runs down to the water.","good":"The garden runs down to the water."},{"bad":"A friendly black Labrador greets every visitor.","good":"A friendly black Labrador greets every visitor."},{"bad":"We visit them every summer.","good":"We visit them every summer."}]},
      {"bad":"The team designed a new building. The architect proposed a tall glass modern tower. The council approved the plan. Workers cleared a large empty grey site. The building opened three years later.","good":"The team designed a new building. The architect proposed a tall modern glass tower. The council approved the plan. Workers cleared a large grey empty site. The building opened three years later.","explanation":"Order: size, shape, age (\"a large grey empty site\") and size, age, material (\"tall modern glass tower\").","sentences":[{"bad":"The team designed a new building.","good":"The team designed a new building."},{"bad":"The architect proposed a tall glass modern tower.","good":"The architect proposed a tall modern glass tower."},{"bad":"The council approved the plan.","good":"The council approved the plan."},{"bad":"Workers cleared a large empty grey site.","good":"Workers cleared a large grey empty site."},{"bad":"The building opened three years later.","good":"The building opened three years later."}]}
