    "7.2": [
      {"bad":"The two sisters both love running. Anna is more taller than her sister. She trains three times a week. Her times are getting more better every month. The coach expects a strong season.","good":"The two sisters both love running. Anna is taller than her sister. She trains three times a week. Her times are getting better every month. The coach expects a strong season.","explanation":"Use only one comparative marker: \"taller\", \"better\" (never \"more taller\").","sentences":[{"bad":"The two sisters both love running.","good":"The two sisters both love running."},{"bad":"Anna is more taller than her sister.","good":"Anna is taller than her sister."},{"bad":"She trains three times a week.","good":"She trains three times a week."},{"bad":"Her times are getting more better every month.","good":"Her times are getting better every month."},{"bad":"The coach expects a strong season.","good":"The coach expects a strong season."}]},
      {"bad":"The city has two main bridges. The new bridge is more wider than the old one. It carries traffic in both directions. The old bridge is more narrower. Both bridges are busy at rush hour.","good":"The city has two main bridges. The new bridge is wider than the old one. It carries traffic in both directions. The old bridge is narrower. Both bridges are busy at rush hour.","explanation":"Use \"wider\" and \"narrower\", not \"more wider\"/\"more narrower\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The city has two main bridges.","good":"The city has two main bridges."},{"bad":"The new bridge is more wider than the old one.","good":"The new bridge is wider than the old one."},{"bad":"It carries traffic in both directions.","good":"It carries traffic in both directions."},{"bad":"The old bridge is more narrower.","good":"The old bridge is narrower."},{"bad":"Both bridges are busy at rush hour.","good":"Both bridges are busy at rush hour."}]},
      {"bad":"We compared two hotels for our holiday. The seaside hotel was more cheaper. It was also much nearer the beach. The city hotel looked more nicer in the photos. We chose the seaside hotel in the end.","good":"We compared two hotels for our holiday. The seaside hotel was cheaper. It was also much nearer the beach. The city hotel looked nicer in the photos. We chose the seaside hotel in the end.","explanation":"Use \"cheaper\" and \"nicer\" as single comparatives.","sentences":[{"bad":"We compared two hotels for our holiday.","good":"We compared two hotels for our holiday."},{"bad":"The seaside hotel was more cheaper.","good":"The seaside hotel was cheaper."},{"bad":"It was also much nearer the beach.","good":"It was also much nearer the beach."},{"bad":"The city hotel looked more nicer in the photos.","good":"The city hotel looked nicer in the photos."},{"bad":"We chose the seaside hotel in the end.","good":"We chose the seaside hotel in the end."}]},
      {"bad":"My brother and I both play chess. He is more cleverer than me at the game. He practises against the computer. His openings are more stronger now. I am slowly catching up.","good":"My brother and I both play chess. He is cleverer than me at the game. He practises against the computer. His openings are stronger now. I am slowly catching up.","explanation":"Use \"cleverer\" and \"stronger\", not double comparatives.","sentences":[{"bad":"My brother and I both play chess.","good":"My brother and I both play chess."},{"bad":"He is more cleverer than me at the game.","good":"He is cleverer than me at the game."},{"bad":"He practises against the computer.","good":"He practises against the computer."},{"bad":"His openings are more stronger now.","good":"His openings are stronger now."},{"bad":"I am slowly catching up.","good":"I am slowly catching up."}]},
      {"bad":"The town built two new pools. The outdoor pool is more bigger. It opens only in summer. The indoor pool is more busier in winter. Both pools are popular with families.","good":"The town built two new pools. The outdoor pool is bigger. It opens only in summer. The indoor pool is busier in winter. Both pools are popular with families.","explanation":"Use \"bigger\" and \"busier\" as single comparatives.","sentences":[{"bad":"The town built two new pools.","good":"The town built two new pools."},{"bad":"The outdoor pool is more bigger.","good":"The outdoor pool is bigger."},{"bad":"It opens only in summer.","good":"It opens only in summer."},{"bad":"The indoor pool is more busier in winter.","good":"The indoor pool is busier in winter."},{"bad":"Both pools are popular with families.","good":"Both pools are popular with families."}]}
