    "7.6": [
      {"bad":"My colleague answered the phone. She speaks always politely to customers. She has worked here for years. She drinks never coffee after noon. Her cheerful manner is well known.","good":"My colleague answered the phone. She always speaks politely to customers. She has worked here for years. She never drinks coffee after noon. Her cheerful manner is well known.","explanation":"Frequency adverbs go before the main verb: \"always speaks\", \"never drinks\".","sentences":[{"bad":"My colleague answered the phone.","good":"My colleague answered the phone."},{"bad":"She speaks always politely to customers.","good":"She always speaks politely to customers."},{"bad":"She has worked here for years.","good":"She has worked here for years."},{"bad":"She drinks never coffee after noon.","good":"She never drinks coffee after noon."},{"bad":"Her cheerful manner is well known.","good":"Her cheerful manner is well known."}]},
      {"bad":"The bus arrives at the same time. It is usually busy in the morning. Many commuters take it daily. They have often to stand in the aisle. The journey takes forty minutes.","good":"The bus arrives at the same time. It is usually busy in the morning. Many commuters take it daily. They often have to stand in the aisle. The journey takes forty minutes.","explanation":"Place \"usually\" after \"is\" and \"often\" before \"have\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The bus arrives at the same time.","good":"The bus arrives at the same time."},{"bad":"It is usually busy in the morning.","good":"It is usually busy in the morning."},{"bad":"Many commuters take it daily.","good":"Many commuters take it daily."},{"bad":"They have often to stand in the aisle.","good":"They often have to stand in the aisle."},{"bad":"The journey takes forty minutes.","good":"The journey takes forty minutes."}]},
      {"bad":"The twins finish their homework early. They do always their chores first. Their parents are very proud. They are never late for dinner. The family eats together each evening.","good":"The twins finish their homework early. They always do their chores first. Their parents are very proud. They are never late for dinner. The family eats together each evening.","explanation":"Frequency adverbs go between the subject and verb, after \"be\": \"always do\", \"are never\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The twins finish their homework early.","good":"The twins finish their homework early."},{"bad":"They do always their chores first.","good":"They always do their chores first."},{"bad":"Their parents are very proud.","good":"Their parents are very proud."},{"bad":"They are never late for dinner.","good":"They are never late for dinner."},{"bad":"The family eats together each evening.","good":"The family eats together each evening."}]},
      {"bad":"The gardener tends the flower beds. She checks often the roses for pests. The roses bloom twice a year. She waters the plants rarely in autumn. The garden wins prizes each summer.","good":"The gardener tends the flower beds. She often checks the roses for pests. The roses bloom twice a year. She rarely waters the plants in autumn. The garden wins prizes each summer.","explanation":"Place the adverb before the main verb: \"often checks\", \"rarely waters\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The gardener tends the flower beds.","good":"The gardener tends the flower beds."},{"bad":"She checks often the roses for pests.","good":"She often checks the roses for pests."},{"bad":"The roses bloom twice a year.","good":"The roses bloom twice a year."},{"bad":"She waters the plants rarely in autumn.","good":"She rarely waters the plants in autumn."},{"bad":"The garden wins prizes each summer.","good":"The garden wins prizes each summer."}]},
      {"bad":"The staff open the shop at nine. They always are friendly to customers. The manager greets everyone warmly. He never has missed a day of work. The shop has a loyal following.","good":"The staff open the shop at nine. They are always friendly to customers. The manager greets everyone warmly. He has never missed a day of work. The shop has a loyal following.","explanation":"After \"be\" and \"have\" place the adverb: \"are always\", \"has never\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The staff open the shop at nine.","good":"The staff open the shop at nine."},{"bad":"They always are friendly to customers.","good":"They are always friendly to customers."},{"bad":"The manager greets everyone warmly.","good":"The manager greets everyone warmly."},{"bad":"He never has missed a day of work.","good":"He has never missed a day of work."},{"bad":"The shop has a loyal following.","good":"The shop has a loyal following."}]}
