    "7.7": [
      {"bad":"We compared the weather of two seasons. This summer is hotter than last summer. The gardens need more water than before. The evenings are warmer than in May. We spend much more time outdoors now.","good":"We compared the weather of two seasons. This summer is hotter than last summer was. The gardens need more water than before. The evenings are warmer than they were in May. We spend much more time outdoors now.","explanation":"Compare like with like: \"than last summer was\", \"than they were in May\".","sentences":[{"bad":"We compared the weather of two seasons.","good":"We compared the weather of two seasons."},{"bad":"This summer is hotter than last summer.","good":"This summer is hotter than last summer was."},{"bad":"The gardens need more water than before.","good":"The gardens need more water than before."},{"bad":"The evenings are warmer than in May.","good":"The evenings are warmer than they were in May."},{"bad":"We spend much more time outdoors now.","good":"We spend much more time outdoors now."}]},
      {"bad":"My friends enjoy different hobbies. Swimming is more fun than to run. Both keep you fit. Reading is quieter than to watch television. Everyone has their own favourite.","good":"My friends enjoy different hobbies. Swimming is more fun than running. Both keep you fit. Reading is quieter than watching television. Everyone has their own favourite.","explanation":"Keep the two compared items parallel: gerund with gerund.","sentences":[{"bad":"My friends enjoy different hobbies.","good":"My friends enjoy different hobbies."},{"bad":"Swimming is more fun than to run.","good":"Swimming is more fun than running."},{"bad":"Both keep you fit.","good":"Both keep you fit."},{"bad":"Reading is quieter than to watch television.","good":"Reading is quieter than watching television."},{"bad":"Everyone has their own favourite.","good":"Everyone has their own favourite."}]},
      {"bad":"The two routes differ in difficulty. Cycling is faster than to walk. The cycle path is smooth and flat. Walking is safer than to ride on the main road. We chose the cycle path anyway.","good":"The two routes differ in difficulty. Cycling is faster than walking. The cycle path is smooth and flat. Walking is safer than riding on the main road. We chose the cycle path anyway.","explanation":"Use parallel gerunds after \"than\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The two routes differ in difficulty.","good":"The two routes differ in difficulty."},{"bad":"Cycling is faster than to walk.","good":"Cycling is faster than walking."},{"bad":"The cycle path is smooth and flat.","good":"The cycle path is smooth and flat."},{"bad":"Walking is safer than to ride on the main road.","good":"Walking is safer than riding on the main road."},{"bad":"We chose the cycle path anyway.","good":"We chose the cycle path anyway."}]},
      {"bad":"The town compared its two parks. The riverside park is greener than the square. It also has a larger playground. The play area is busier than last year. Families visit it all summer.","good":"The town compared its two parks. The riverside park is greener than the square is. It also has a larger playground. The play area is busier than it was last year. Families visit it all summer.","explanation":"Compare clause with clause: \"than the square is\", \"than it was last year\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The town compared its two parks.","good":"The town compared its two parks."},{"bad":"The riverside park is greener than the square.","good":"The riverside park is greener than the square is."},{"bad":"It also has a larger playground.","good":"It also has a larger playground."},{"bad":"The play area is busier than last year.","good":"The play area is busier than it was last year."},{"bad":"Families visit it all summer.","good":"Families visit it all summer."}]},
      {"bad":"Two students discussed their subjects. History is more interesting than to study maths. Both require plenty of reading. Essays are easier than to sit exams for some people. They each chose their favourite.","good":"Two students discussed their subjects. History is more interesting than studying maths. Both require plenty of reading. Essays are easier than sitting exams for some people. They each chose their favourite.","explanation":"Keep the comparison parallel: \"studying maths\", \"sitting exams\".","sentences":[{"bad":"Two students discussed their subjects.","good":"Two students discussed their subjects."},{"bad":"History is more interesting than to study maths.","good":"History is more interesting than studying maths."},{"bad":"Both require plenty of reading.","good":"Both require plenty of reading."},{"bad":"Essays are easier than to sit exams for some people.","good":"Essays are easier than sitting exams for some people."},{"bad":"They each chose their favourite.","good":"They each chose their favourite."}]}
    ],
    "8.1": [
      {"bad":"My cousin was born in a small hospital. She was born in a cold Monday morning. The family celebrated for days. They gather every year at that same day. The story is retold at every birthday.","good":"My cousin was born in a small hospital. She was born on a cold Monday morning. The family celebrated for days. They gather every year on that same day. The story is retold at every birthday.","explanation":"Use \"on\" with days and dates: \"on a Monday morning\", \"on that day\".","sentences":[{"bad":"My cousin was born in a small hospital.","good":"My cousin was born in a small hospital."},{"bad":"She was born in a cold Monday morning.","good":"She was born on a cold Monday morning."},{"bad":"The family celebrated for days.","good":"The family celebrated for days."},{"bad":"They gather every year at that same day.","good":"They gather every year on that same day."},{"bad":"The story is retold at every birthday.","good":"The story is retold at every birthday."}]},
      {"bad":"We start school early each day. Lessons begin at the morning. The first break comes at ten. The hall is quiet at the afternoon. Clubs run after lessons end.","good":"We start school early each day. Lessons begin in the morning. The first break comes at ten. The hall is quiet in the afternoon. Clubs run after lessons end.","explanation":"Use \"in\" with parts of the day: \"in the morning\", \"in the afternoon\".","sentences":[{"bad":"We start school early each day.","good":"We start school early each day."},{"bad":"Lessons begin at the morning.","good":"Lessons begin in the morning."},{"bad":"The first break comes at ten.","good":"The first break comes at ten."},{"bad":"The hall is quiet at the afternoon.","good":"The hall is quiet in the afternoon."},{"bad":"Clubs run after lessons end.","good":"Clubs run after lessons end."}]},
      {"bad":"My parents first met at university. They met at the year 1998. They married two years later. The wedding was at a warm June day. They still celebrate every year.","good":"My parents first met at university. They met in the year 1998. They married two years later. The wedding was on a warm June day. They still celebrate every year.","explanation":"Use \"in\" with years and \"on\" with days.","sentences":[{"bad":"My parents first met at university.","good":"My parents first met at university."},{"bad":"They met at the year 1998.","good":"They met in the year 1998."},{"bad":"They married two years later.","good":"They married two years later."},{"bad":"The wedding was at a warm June day.","good":"The wedding was on a warm June day."},{"bad":"They still celebrate every year.","good":"They still celebrate every year."}]},
      {"bad":"The train stops at several towns. We arrived to the station early. The platform was busy. We waited in the platform for the train. The train left on time.","good":"The train stops at several towns. We arrived at the station early. The platform was busy. We waited on the platform for the train. The train left on time.","explanation":"Use \"arrive at\" and, for a raised surface, \"on the platform\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The train stops at several towns.","good":"The train stops at several towns."},{"bad":"We arrived to the station early.","good":"We arrived at the station early."},{"bad":"The platform was busy.","good":"The platform was busy."},{"bad":"We waited in the platform for the train.","good":"We waited on the platform for the train."},{"bad":"The train left on time.","good":"The train left on time."}]},
      {"bad":"The picture shows an old street. A lamp stands in the corner of the room. A rug lies in the middle of the floor. Some keys hang at the wall. The street looks quiet and still.","good":"The picture shows an old street. A lamp stands in the corner of the room. A rug lies in the middle of the floor. Some keys hang on the wall. The street looks quiet and still.","explanation":"Use \"on the wall\" for a surface, \"in the corner\" for an enclosed space.","sentences":[{"bad":"The picture shows an old street.","good":"The picture shows an old street."},{"bad":"A lamp stands in the corner of the room.","good":"A lamp stands in the corner of the room."},{"bad":"A rug lies in the middle of the floor.","good":"A rug lies in the middle of the floor."},{"bad":"Some keys hang at the wall.","good":"Some keys hang on the wall."},{"bad":"The street looks quiet and still.","good":"The street looks quiet and still."}]}
