    "9.1": [
      {"bad":"The school holds a fair every summer. The children plays games on the field. Parents watch from the shade. Our dog bark at every visitor. The fair lasts the whole afternoon.","good":"The school holds a fair every summer. The children play games on the field. Parents watch from the shade. Our dog barks at every visitor. The fair lasts the whole afternoon.","explanation":"A singular subject takes \"barks\"; a plural subject takes \"play\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The school holds a fair every summer.","good":"The school holds a fair every summer."},{"bad":"The children plays games on the field.","good":"The children play games on the field."},{"bad":"Parents watch from the shade.","good":"Parents watch from the shade."},{"bad":"Our dog bark at every visitor.","good":"Our dog barks at every visitor."},{"bad":"The fair lasts the whole afternoon.","good":"The fair lasts the whole afternoon."}]},
      {"bad":"The café opens early each day. The waiters serves breakfast from seven. The tables fill quickly. A young chef cook the eggs. The smell draws people inside.","good":"The café opens early each day. The waiters serve breakfast from seven. The tables fill quickly. A young chef cooks the eggs. The smell draws people inside.","explanation":"Use \"serve\" with a plural subject and \"cooks\" with a singular one.","sentences":[{"bad":"The café opens early each day.","good":"The café opens early each day."},{"bad":"The waiters serves breakfast from seven.","good":"The waiters serve breakfast from seven."},{"bad":"The tables fill quickly.","good":"The tables fill quickly."},{"bad":"A young chef cook the eggs.","good":"A young chef cooks the eggs."},{"bad":"The smell draws people inside.","good":"The smell draws people inside."}]},
      {"bad":"The library lends books for free. The shelves holds thousands of titles. Readers browse in the quiet room. A single lamp light the reading desk. The library closes at six.","good":"The library lends books for free. The shelves hold thousands of titles. Readers browse in the quiet room. A single lamp lights the reading desk. The library closes at six.","explanation":"Agreement: \"shelves hold\" but \"lamp lights\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The library lends books for free.","good":"The library lends books for free."},{"bad":"The shelves holds thousands of titles.","good":"The shelves hold thousands of titles."},{"bad":"Readers browse in the quiet room.","good":"Readers browse in the quiet room."},{"bad":"A single lamp light the reading desk.","good":"A single lamp lights the reading desk."},{"bad":"The library closes at six.","good":"The library closes at six."}]},
      {"bad":"The team trains twice a week. The players runs around the track. The coach blows the whistle. A new member join every month. The team improves each season.","good":"The team trains twice a week. The players run around the track. The coach blows the whistle. A new member joins every month. The team improves each season.","explanation":"Use \"players run\" and \"member joins\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The team trains twice a week.","good":"The team trains twice a week."},{"bad":"The players runs around the track.","good":"The players run around the track."},{"bad":"The coach blows the whistle.","good":"The coach blows the whistle."},{"bad":"A new member join every month.","good":"A new member joins every month."},{"bad":"The team improves each season.","good":"The team improves each season."}]},
      {"bad":"The garden blooms in late spring. The roses opens before the tulips. Bees visit the flowers daily. A robin sings from the fence. The whole garden feels alive.","good":"The garden blooms in late spring. The roses open before the tulips. Bees visit the flowers daily. A robin sings from the fence. The whole garden feels alive.","explanation":"Use \"roses open\" with the plural subject.","sentences":[{"bad":"The garden blooms in late spring.","good":"The garden blooms in late spring."},{"bad":"The roses opens before the tulips.","good":"The roses open before the tulips."},{"bad":"Bees visit the flowers daily.","good":"Bees visit the flowers daily."},{"bad":"A robin sings from the fence.","good":"A robin sings from the fence."},{"bad":"The whole garden feels alive.","good":"The whole garden feels alive."}]}
