      {"bad":"The team packed for the trip. They took boots gloves and hats. The forecast promised cold weather. They added snacks water and a map. Their rucksacks were ready.","good":"The team packed for the trip. They took boots, gloves and hats. The forecast promised cold weather. They added snacks, water and a map. Their rucksacks were ready.","explanation":"Use commas between the items of a list.","sentences":[{"bad":"The team packed for the trip.","good":"The team packed for the trip."},{"bad":"They took boots gloves and hats.","good":"They took boots, gloves and hats."},{"bad":"The forecast promised cold weather.","good":"The forecast promised cold weather."},{"bad":"They added snacks water and a map.","good":"They added snacks, water and a map."},{"bad":"Their rucksacks were ready.","good":"Their rucksacks were ready."}]},
      {"bad":"The garden needed several jobs done. She mowed trimmed and watered the lawn. The flower beds looked neat. She planted roses tulips and daisies. The garden was lovely by evening.","good":"The garden needed several jobs done. She mowed, trimmed and watered the lawn. The flower beds looked neat. She planted roses, tulips and daisies. The garden was lovely by evening.","explanation":"Separate the listed verbs and nouns with commas.","sentences":[{"bad":"The garden needed several jobs done.","good":"The garden needed several jobs done."},{"bad":"She mowed trimmed and watered the lawn.","good":"She mowed, trimmed and watered the lawn."},{"bad":"The flower beds looked neat.","good":"The flower beds looked neat."},{"bad":"She planted roses tulips and daisies.","good":"She planted roses, tulips and daisies."},{"bad":"The garden was lovely by evening.","good":"The garden was lovely by evening."}]},
      {"bad":"The class prepared a display. They painted drew and printed their work. The wall looked colourful. They added photos posters and charts. The display won a school prize.","good":"The class prepared a display. They painted, drew and printed their work. The wall looked colourful. They added photos, posters and charts. The display won a school prize.","explanation":"Use commas to separate items in a list.","sentences":[{"bad":"The class prepared a display.","good":"The class prepared a display."},{"bad":"They painted drew and printed their work.","good":"They painted, drew and printed their work."},{"bad":"The wall looked colourful.","good":"The wall looked colourful."},{"bad":"They added photos posters and charts.","good":"They added photos, posters and charts."},{"bad":"The display won a school prize.","good":"The display won a school prize."}]},
