    "10.6": [
      {"bad":"The cat slept on the sofa. The cat licked it's paw. It looked very content. Its raining outside now. The cat moved to a warmer spot.","good":"The cat slept on the sofa. The cat licked its paw. It looked very content. It's raining outside now. The cat moved to a warmer spot.","explanation":"\"Its\" shows possession; \"it's\" means \"it is\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The cat slept on the sofa.","good":"The cat slept on the sofa."},{"bad":"The cat licked it's paw.","good":"The cat licked its paw."},{"bad":"It looked very content.","good":"It looked very content."},{"bad":"Its raining outside now.","good":"It's raining outside now."},{"bad":"The cat moved to a warmer spot.","good":"The cat moved to a warmer spot."}]},
      {"bad":"The robot needed a new battery. The machine lost it's power. The technician opened the panel. Its going to take an hour to fix. The robot was soon working again.","good":"The robot needed a new battery. The machine lost its power. The technician opened the panel. It's going to take an hour to fix. The robot was soon working again.","explanation":"Use \"its\" for possession and \"it's\" for \"it is\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The robot needed a new battery.","good":"The robot needed a new battery."},{"bad":"The machine lost it's power.","good":"The machine lost its power."},{"bad":"The technician opened the panel.","good":"The technician opened the panel."},{"bad":"Its going to take an hour to fix.","good":"It's going to take an hour to fix."},{"bad":"The robot was soon working again.","good":"The robot was soon working again."}]},
      {"bad":"The tree lost all of its leaves. The old oak shed it's leaves early. The branches stood bare. Its a sign that winter is coming. The garden will sleep until spring.","good":"The tree lost all of its leaves. The old oak shed its leaves early. The branches stood bare. It's a sign that winter is coming. The garden will sleep until spring.","explanation":"\"Its leaves\" (possession) versus \"It's a sign\" (it is).","sentences":[{"bad":"The tree lost all of its leaves.","good":"The tree lost all of its leaves."},{"bad":"The old oak shed it's leaves early.","good":"The old oak shed its leaves early."},{"bad":"The branches stood bare.","good":"The branches stood bare."},{"bad":"Its a sign that winter is coming.","good":"It's a sign that winter is coming."},{"bad":"The garden will sleep until spring.","good":"The garden will sleep until spring."}]},
      {"bad":"The school has a new hall. The building had it's roof repaired. The work took three months. Its much brighter inside now. The pupils love the new space.","good":"The school has a new hall. The building had its roof repaired. The work took three months. It's much brighter inside now. The pupils love the new space.","explanation":"Use \"its roof\" for possession and \"It's\" for \"it is\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The school has a new hall.","good":"The school has a new hall."},{"bad":"The building had it's roof repaired.","good":"The building had its roof repaired."},{"bad":"The work took three months.","good":"The work took three months."},{"bad":"Its much brighter inside now.","good":"It's much brighter inside now."},{"bad":"The pupils love the new space.","good":"The pupils love the new space."}]},
      {"bad":"The puppy chased its own tail. The puppy wagged it's tail happily. It ran around the garden. Its tired now after all that play. It curled up for a nap.","good":"The puppy chased its own tail. The puppy wagged its tail happily. It ran around the garden. It's tired now after all that play. It curled up for a nap.","explanation":"\"Its tail\" (possession) and \"It's tired\" (it is).","sentences":[{"bad":"The puppy chased its own tail.","good":"The puppy chased its own tail."},{"bad":"The puppy wagged it's tail happily.","good":"The puppy wagged its tail happily."},{"bad":"It ran around the garden.","good":"It ran around the garden."},{"bad":"Its tired now after all that play.","good":"It's tired now after all that play."},{"bad":"It curled up for a nap.","good":"It curled up for a nap."}]}
