      {"bad":"The town held a food festival. A family run bakery won first prize. The judges tasted many entries. The award went to a hand made cake. The festival was a great success.","good":"The town held a food festival. A family-run bakery won first prize. The judges tasted many entries. The award went to a hand-made cake. The festival was a great success.","explanation":"Hyphenate \"family-run\" and \"hand-made\" before nouns.","sentences":[{"bad":"The town held a food festival.","good":"The town held a food festival."},{"bad":"A family run bakery won first prize.","good":"A family-run bakery won first prize."},{"bad":"The judges tasted many entries.","good":"The judges tasted many entries."},{"bad":"The award went to a hand made cake.","good":"The award went to a hand-made cake."},{"bad":"The festival was a great success.","good":"The festival was a great success."}]},
