      {"bad":"My cousins moved to a new town. Their house is near the park. They like the neighbourhood. There coming to visit us next month. We will meet them at the station.","good":"My cousins moved to a new town. Their house is near the park. They like the neighbourhood. They're coming to visit us next month. We will meet them at the station.","explanation":"Use \"They're\" for \"they are\" and \"their\" for possession.","sentences":[{"bad":"My cousins moved to a new town.","good":"My cousins moved to a new town."},{"bad":"Their house is near the park.","good":"Their house is near the park."},{"bad":"They like the neighbourhood.","good":"They like the neighbourhood."},{"bad":"There coming to visit us next month.","good":"They're coming to visit us next month."},{"bad":"We will meet them at the station.","good":"We will meet them at the station."}]},
      {"bad":"The students finished the project. There results were excellent. The teacher praised the whole class. Their going to celebrate on Friday. The party is at the café.","good":"The students finished the project. Their results were excellent. The teacher praised the whole class. They're going to celebrate on Friday. The party is at the café.","explanation":"\"Their results\" (possession) and \"They're going\" (they are).","sentences":[{"bad":"The students finished the project.","good":"The students finished the project."},{"bad":"There results were excellent.","good":"Their results were excellent."},{"bad":"The teacher praised the whole class.","good":"The teacher praised the whole class."},{"bad":"Their going to celebrate on Friday.","good":"They're going to celebrate on Friday."},{"bad":"The party is at the café.","good":"The party is at the café."}]},
      {"bad":"The birds built a nest in the tree. There nest is high in the branches. They return to it each spring. Their singing every morning. The garden is full of birdsong.","good":"The birds built a nest in the tree. Their nest is high in the branches. They return to it each spring. They're singing every morning. The garden is full of birdsong.","explanation":"Use \"their nest\" (possession) and \"They're singing\" (they are).","sentences":[{"bad":"The birds built a nest in the tree.","good":"The birds built a nest in the tree."},{"bad":"There nest is high in the branches.","good":"Their nest is high in the branches."},{"bad":"They return to it each spring.","good":"They return to it each spring."},{"bad":"Their singing every morning.","good":"They're singing every morning."},{"bad":"The garden is full of birdsong.","good":"The garden is full of birdsong."}]},
